# netsurf: a box kept for the full reconvert is normalised (patch 509)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 508)
#
# The census at 507 found Wikipedia (en.m, PlayStation_Vita) asserting in
# layout_minmax_table (cell->type == BOX_TABLE_CELL) on 2 of 3 loads;
# bisected to patch 506 (502-505 0 of 12 loads, 506 3 of 3). 506 only
# changed which path took a batch: the bug is patch 374's. A local builder
# that gives up after its new boxes fetched an object keeps them where
# box_build_element put them, for the full reconvert -- unnormalised, under
# their DOM parent's box. Wikipedia's #toc is display: table; its
# .toctitle flex box, rebuilt whole (a child list the flex path declined),
# landed beside the table's anonymous row group, and when the toggle's SVG
# arrived before the full reconvert ran (html_object_callback ->
# html_reformat), layout read the flex box as a row group.
#
# html_rl_kept_normalise: the kept box's enclosing table (through row groups
# and rows) is normalised again, as a full build makes it (the anonymous row
# group, row and cell around it; normalised boxes come through unchanged);
# anywhere else the new subtree itself is normalised.
#
# Simulator-only test hook (VITA_HOST_SIM, as patch 473's): a page whose
# <html> carries data-vb-reformat-queued is laid out, every min/max width
# measured again, just before macos9_reconvert asks for the full reconvert
# -- the window an arriving object found. Gate: JS-kept-table /
# CSS-kept-table-ref (without the fix the page asserts as Wikipedia did;
# with it 0 rows differ). Wikipedia: 4 of 4 loads clean, the table
# normalised once per load.
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c
